[[File:Will to Fight (Beta 33.0).png|thumb|293x293px|Beta 33.0]]
Before '''Beta 4.1''', this card added ATK to a monster equal to its missing HP. This made it possible for cards such as [[Ice]] to get down to 1 HP, have Will to Fight applied to it, and then gain an additional 6 ATK. This costed 3G.
[[File:Will to Fight (Beta 48.0).png|thumb|291x291px|Beta 48.0]]
This was at times far too powerful when combined with [http://undercards.wikia.com/wiki/Same_Fate Same Fate], and was reworked in Beta 4.1 as a result. Now, it can only select an ally monster and will send it back to your deck with +4/+4. The cost was reduced to 2G, but was reduced to 1G in '''Beta 4.3'''.

'''Beta 6.2''' buffed it by also making you draw a card, much like what happened with spells of other classes, like [http://undercards.wikia.com/wiki/Heal Heal], [http://undercards.wikia.com/wiki/Poison Poison] and [http://undercards.wikia.com/wiki/Protection Protection]. This was removed in '''Beta 10.2''', though.

'''Beta 48.0''' reworked the class and most of its spells, this included. Its cost returned to 3G and will now add a random [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Angel_of_Death Lost Soul] to the top of your deck with +2/+2 and Haste. '''Beta 48.1''' made DT's Passive and some of its spells no longer give Lost Souls randomly, but instead in a specific order. This was one of those spells.

=== Stats ===
Soul Type: Determination

Cost:
* 3 (Post Alpha 3.0)
* 2 (Post Beta 4.1)
